To obtain an Adult Entertainment Business License, an Applicant must submit to the City Administrator a completed, sworn License Application containing the following information:
A. If the Applicant is:
1. An individual, the individual's legal name, aliases, date of birth, and mailing address;
2. A partnership, the full and complete name of the partnership, whether the partnership is general or limited, a copy of the partnership agreement (if any), and the legal names, dates of birth, aliases and mailing addresses of each partner;
3. A corporation, the corporation's exact and complete corporate name, the date of its incorporation, evidence that the corporation is registered to do business in and in good standing with the State of Georgia, the legal name, date of birth, aliases, mailing address and corporate title of each officer and director and of each stockholder, the name and address of the registered Agent for service of process, and the address of the principal business office of the corporation;
4. Other entity, the full and complete name of the entity, whether the entity is for profit or not for profit, a copy of the document that creates the entity or establishes the rights and duties of the owners of the entity, or if no such document exists, a document that recites the rights and duties of the owners and the legal names, dates of birth, aliases and mailing addresses of each and every person who has any ownership interest in the entity or who will benefit or profit in any way from the conduct of the business; or
5. Regardless of the form of ownership of the Applicant, the legal names, dates of birth, aliases and mailing addresses of each and every person who is a beneficial or equitable owner of the Business, being defined as any person who enjoys the rights and benefits incident to ownership, whether or not legal title evidences such ownership;
B. The full true name and any other names used by the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s);
C. The present address and telephone number of the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s);
D. The previous addresses of the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s), if any, for a period of five (5) years immediately prior to the date of the application and the dates of residence at each;
E. Acceptable written proof that the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s) are at least eighteen (18) years of age;
F. The height, weight, color of eyes and hair and date and place of birth of the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s).
G. Two photographs of the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s) at least two (2) inches by two (2) inches taken within the last six (6) months; (and in addition, the applicant and the operator(s) must agree to be photographed by the City police department prior to issuance of the license applied for);
H. The business, occupation or employment history of the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s) for the five (5) years immediately preceding the date of application;
I. The business license history of the applicant and whether such applicant, in previous operations in this or any other location under license, has had such license or permit for an Adult Entertainment Business or similar type of business revoked or suspended, the reason therefore, and the business activity or occupation subsequent to such action of revocation or suspension;
J. If the application is made on behalf of a corporation, the name of the corporation, exactly as shown in its articles of incorporation or charter, together with the place and date of incorporation. If the application is on behalf of a limited partnership, a copy of the certificate of limited partnership shall be provided. If one (1) or more of the partners is a corporation, the provisions of this subsection pertaining to corporations shall apply to each such corporation;
K. The names and addresses of the owner and if applicable, the lessor of the real property upon which the adult entertainment establishment is to be operated, engaged in, conducted or carried on and a copy of the lease or rental agreement, if any;
L. With respect to the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s), all convictions, (excluding misdemeanor traffic violations unrelated to driving under the influence of drugs or alcohol) within the past ten (10) years, including a complete description of the crime or violation, the date of the crime or violation, date of conviction (including plea of guilty or nolo contendere), jurisdiction and any disposition including any fine or sentence imposed and whether the terms of disposition have been fully completed. Each person required to disclose convictions hereunder shall also provide a signed and notarized consent, on forms prescribed by the Georgia Crime Information Center, authorizing the release of his or her criminal records to the City police department.
M. A complete set of fingerprints of the applicant and the operator(s);
O. If the person or business entity on whose behalf application for a license is doing business under a trade name, a copy of the trade name as properly recorded. If the application is made on behalf of a corporation, a copy of its authority to do business in the state should be provided, including articles of incorporation, and a trade name affidavit, if any, and last annual report, if any;
P. The address of the premises where the adult entertainment establishment will be operated, engaged in, conducted, or carried on;
Q. Whether the Applicant or any individual identified in response to subsection (A) above has been issued or has applied for a license to operate an Adult Entertainment Business in the City of McDonough or in any other jurisdiction; and, if so, the name in which the license was issued or applied for; the date any such license was granted or, if not granted, applied for; the business location for which license was issued or applied for; the current status of the application or license; and, if applicable, the date and circumstances of any application denial, license suspension or license revocation or other administrative action;
R. A site plan and a certified survey drawn to appropriate scale of the proposed Adult Entertainment Facility indicating at least all property lines, rights-of-way, location of buildings, parking areas and spaces, curb cuts, driveways and distances to the following:
1. The nearest parcel of land used or zoned for residential use;
2. The nearest parcel of land upon which any facility of worship, school, library, civic center, public park, hospital, child care business, community club, jail, prison or building owned or operated by any governmental or quasi-governmental entity is located;
3. The nearest parcel of land upon which another facility regulated or defined under this Chapter is located; and
4. The nearest parcel of land upon which an establishment selling alcoholic beverages, beer or wine or consumption of same on the premises; is located.
S. A floor plan drawn to appropriate scale of the proposed facility indicating, but not limited to:
1. All windows, all doors, all entrances and exits; and
2. All fixed structural and interior features, including but not limited to doors, walls, stages, partitions, dressing rooms, and private areas.
T. Each application for an adult entertainment establishment license shall be verified and acknowledged under oath to be true and correct by:
1. If application is made on behalf of an individual, the individual;
2. If application is made on behalf of a partnership, by a general partner;
3. If application is made on behalf of a corporation, by the president or chief executive officer of the corporation; and
4. If application is made on behalf of any other organization or association, by the chief administrative official.
(Ord. No. 10-06-07(B), § I, 6-7-2010)

