The applicant shall personally appear before the City Administrator or his designee with payment of the nonrefundable application fee in the amount established by the governing body of the City, and shall present the application containing the aforementioned and described information. The City shall have thirty (30) days from the date of actual receipt of a fully completed application to investigate the facts provided in the application and the background of the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s). The City Administrator or his designee shall stamp the date of receipt of each application on the first page thereof and shall provide the applicant a photocopy of the stamped first page signifying the date of receipt of the application. The City Administrator shall approve or deny the completed application for an adult entertainment establishment license within thirty (30) days of actual receipt of a fully completed application. If any application is received that is not fully complete for any reason, then in such event, the incomplete application shall be returned to the applicant as soon as possible following the discovery of the incompleteness, and the applicant shall be required to submit a newly completed application along with payment of an additional application fee in an amount established by the governing body of the City, and the thirty (30) day time period specified above shall begin over again upon the actual receipt of the fully completed application.
The application for an adult entertainment establishment license shall be granted if the City Administrator finds:
1. The required license application fee has been paid;
2. The application contains all of the information provided for in section above, and the applicant has made no material misrepresentation of fact in the application;
3. Neither the applicant nor any of the operator(s) or owner(s) has been convicted or pled guilty or entered a plea of nolo contendere to any crime involving keeping a place of prostitution, pandering, pimping, public indecency, prostitution, sodomy, solicitation of sodomy, masturbation for hire, sexual battery, rape, child molestation, enticing a child for indecent purposes, or any offense included in the definition of a "criminal offense against a victim who is a minor" as defined in O.C.G.A. § 42-1-12 within a period of ten (10) years next preceding the date of the application. If there has been any such conviction or plea, then the application shall be denied. For purposes of this Chapter, a conviction or plea of guilty or nolo contendere shall be ignored as to any offense for which the applicant was allowed to avail himself of the Georgia First Offender Act unless the applicant is later adjudicated guilty of having violated the terms of his first offender treatment;
4. Neither the applicant nor any of the operator(s) or owner(s) has had an adult entertainment establishment license or permit revoked for cause by this City or any other municipal corporation or county located in or out of the State of Georgia within the five-year period immediately preceding the date of the application;
5. The building, structure, equipment and location of the premises of the adult entertainment business as proposed by the applicant is in compliance with all applicable laws, including but not limited to health, zoning, distance, fire and safety requirements and standards based on information provided by or through other city departments or Henry County;
6. The applicant, operator(s) and owner(s) are all at least eighteen (18) years of age;
7. The proposed premises will be located at least the minimum distances set forth in this Chapter from any residential use, facility of worship, school, public park or Children's Day Care Facility, any other adult entertainment establishment, and any other establishment licensed by the City to sell alcoholic beverages, beer or wine for consumption on the premises; and
8. The grant of such license will not cause a violation of any law of the State of Georgia or the United States.
The City Administrator shall deny the application for an adult entertainment establishment license if the application fails to meet any requirement contained in this section.
(Ord. No. 10-06-07(B), § I, 6-7-2010)

